   "role": "Spell custody twin + module-dependency manifest; carries the full bind signature and, for synthetic roots, the rebuildable module SOURCES (M3); opt-in user-source TEXT rides beside them (S2).",
   "responsibilities": [
    "captures identity and the full bind signature for one live spell target",
    "captures detached disposal names in resolved execution order without sorting or reapplying book policy",
    "delegates the module-world walk to a single-use CrystalAnalyzer (V3 carrier law)",
    "carries the returned CrystalAnalysisResult and exposes it via delegating properties",
    "captures native per-version resolution capability as a detached replay value",
    "keys its record entry: custody_key is the spell id, or \"<spell_id>@<frame>\" when built with per_frame_custody (the frame read from spell.aetheric_frame)",
    "records the frame kind (spellframe_kind) and, for a contract, the Protocol's module and qualname (spellframe_module, spellframe_qualname) so restore and graft rebind the Protocol rather than a same-named category (0.2.8222, record 4.1.0)",
    "records a managed spell's options as plain values - the mode by name, the limit, the queue timeout and the reset names - only for managed_spell_quantity, so every other payload is unchanged (record 4.2.0, 0.2.8242); managed_spell_options returns them, and the static managed_bind_options(payload) is the one reader the restore and graft lanes replay them through"
   ],
   "owns_state": [
    "_analysis (one carried CrystalAnalysisResult)",
    "_disposal_method_names (ordered recorded values)",
    "_frame_name, _custody_key (the record key)",
    "_spellframe_kind, _spellframe_module, _spellframe_qualname (recorded frame kind)",
    "_managed_spell_mode_name, _managed_spell_limit, _managed_spell_timeout_seconds, _managed_spell_reset_methods (recorded managed options)"
   ],
